{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems","id":1223476,"title":"Using sorcery to make war-golems?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-30T19:13:23-07:00","id":1223476,"title":"Using sorcery to make war-golems?","content":"If a sorcerer wants to produce relatively disposable, slow, clunky \u201cmook mecha\u201d that mortals can use to gain the benefits of Legendary Size and warstrider scale weapons...<br /> <br /> Is that a spell or a working? And what level? Assuming that the physical forms need to be physically crafted (by other spells or skilled mortal labor) before they are enchanted.<br /> <br /> These mook mecha would have no Evocations, no Devastating actions, and worse basic traits in all regards: speed, agility, dexterity, soak, health, strength.<br /> <br /> What should it take to repair these golems from less-than-total destruction? Mundane stone-masonry or blacksmithing, or should the sorceror need to get involved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:45:51-07:00","id":1223486,"title":"","content":"If you're talking about combining a craft project with a sorcerous working in order to produce a mech ... sounds like a job for the First Age artifice rules if ever there was one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:49:33-07:00","id":1223487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1223486#post1223486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're talking about combining a craft project with a sorcerous working in order to produce a mech ... sounds like a job for the First Age artifice rules if ever there was one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for warstriders.<br /> <br /> The point of this is to produce something which cannot be compared to a warstrider without provoking laughter, but which is still no laughing matter for mortals to fight on foot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T20:09:30-07:00","id":1223496,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a working or craft endevor, depending on the ins and outs. I'd say Celestial 1, since were above &quot;Making a weird animal&quot; into &quot;Making something new&quot; territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T22:27:43-07:00","id":1223515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1223487#post1223487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's for warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a number of other things as well; why would First Age Artifice not be appropriate for these war-golems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-31-2018, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T03:32:51-07:00","id":1223563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1223515#post1223515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a number of other things as well; why would First Age Artifice not be appropriate for these war-golems?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTo me, they sound sufficiently crude to not be out of place in the Age of Sorrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T04:30:53-07:00","id":1223571,"title":"","content":"Eh, mookstriders are very much the province of mecha shows, and one of the major qualifiers of FAA is that it's anything that would warp the setting if it was too common. <br /> <br /> So by that metric, mookstriders are firmly FAA territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T05:49:06-07:00","id":1223585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1223571#post1223571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mookstriders</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get more hung up on somebody's shorthand terminology then what actually gets described.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">are very much the province of mecha shows, and one of the major qualifiers of FAA is that it's anything that would warp the setting if it was too common.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI find this reasoning to be fallacious. Neon Genesis Evangelion features beings that resemble behemoths as major antagonists, and it's a mecha show set in the modern day, so does the presence of behemoths inappropriately warp the setting?<br /> <br /> Conversely, does the setting not have a place for the Golem of Prague?<br /> <br /> \u200bA line has to be drawn between something being an animated statue and something being a magic robot. I think that what Sunder the Gold is proposing falls on the side of that line that has a place in the setting as it is, with the lack of powers and the highly limited physical capabilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T05:50:48-07:00","id":1223586,"title":"","content":"Anyway:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems#post1223476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What should it take to repair these golems from less-than-total destruction? Mundane stone-masonry or blacksmithing, or should the sorceror need to get involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that it needs mundane repairs made to the structure, and then a sorcerer knits it back together; I would be inclined to let that be a minor working without an XP cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:11:18-07:00","id":1223595,"title":"","content":"Sorcerors are able to summon battlegroups of First Circle Demons, or elementals. Any golems should be roughly in line with that, if the golems aren\u2019t actually Earth elementals.<br /> <br /> They can still act as mobile armor for mortal soldiers without being so large as to fully qualify for Legendary Size, too. Escaflowne\u2019s melefs were smaller than guymelefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-02-2018, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T10:13:36-07:00","id":1223662,"title":"","content":"Hmm... something with just legendary size, separate health/soak pools and mundane weapon stats might work. I'd let it with celestial spells, and first age artifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T10:34:09-07:00","id":1223668,"title":"","content":"Would the golems 100% have their own stats, or did you still intend to use the warstrider model for Dex and abilities? If not, then it isn't too different from Riding a Tyrant Lizard, or other Legendary Sized creature, only you don't feed them and they are perfectly loyal. I'd say Celestial 2 with decent finesse.<br /> <br /> I'd personally go with them being irreparable, and needing to be redone entirely, reusing whatever remains of the initial mass, with refunded XP of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T15:26:41-07:00","id":1223743,"title":"","content":"Based on the entries in the Workings section, I\u2019d probably say that you could maybe get something that had stats similar to a Yeddim with Terrestrial 2, something significantly combat capable with Celestial 2-3 depending on what other stuff you\u2019re bringing to the table, and rasing multiple units at once is probably Solar.<br /> <br /> I could buy using a Terrestrial 2 Working to impart the ability to move and be controlled to a well constructed body, so I could be taliked into allowing a couple of very successful Craft rolls and a Finesse 3+ Working to create something like what you\u2019re talking about, but I\u2019d still probably make you choose between \u201cLegendary Size\u201d and \u201cbeing moderately combat capable.\u201d <br /> <br /> Ok, thinking on it further, here\u2019s my call<br /> Terrestrial 2 - You can build a Warstrider size piloted golem, but there should be a significant downside. Being \u201cmook-mecha\u201d might be enough of one, depending on exact stats. Running down after awhile might be another good downside.<br /> <br /> Celestial 3 - You should definitely be able to create a giant Golem with magical powers here, but that might be overkill for what you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, it would also depend on the game I was running. If we\u2019re running a Warstrider-OK game already, I\u2019d probably be much more ok with \u201cmook-mecha\u201d running around, so they\u2019d definitely be a Terrestrial 2 Working then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 05-31-2018, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T00:03:01-07:00","id":1224098,"title":"","content":"If its a spell, it would definitely be a celestial one, or a terrestrial one with high drawbacks. You can most definitely make multiple ones with this, and its way too setting breaking for a terrestrial sorcerer to create armies of giant mooks to smash apart mortal armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T07:47:27-07:00","id":1224159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1224098#post1224098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If its a spell, it would definitely be a celestial one, or a terrestrial one with high drawbacks. You can most definitely make multiple ones with this, and its way too setting breaking for a terrestrial sorcerer to create armies of giant mooks to smash apart mortal armies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas it would definitely be setting-reinforcing, for a Dragon-Blooded game with warstriders, to use their ancient and venerable (or new and untested, but powerful) god-machines against mecha-mooks produced by evil Lunar sorcerors, with a final boss fight against a kaiju or a Lunar using their own warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T10:55:59-07:00","id":1224199,"title":"","content":"Given balance concerns and theme, id peg it at Celestial 1-2, depending on level of \u201cmookiness\u201d. If it was Terrestrial, they\u2019d be common in groups like the Realm or Lookshy, who have organized military sorcerer groups. If you wanted something similar for Terrestrial Sorcery, it makes more thematic sense to make Legendary-Size Critters and train handlers to bring them into battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12847-kintani","name":"Kintani","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T19:17:27-07:00","id":1224259,"title":"","content":"If we are using the rules for a walking statue/golem/Automaton on page 500 of the rule book, Terrestrial seems sufficient to me. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solomon_ibn_Gabirol\" target=\"_blank\">Folklore</a> is full of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judah_Loew_ben_Bezalel\" target=\"_blank\">people</a> making <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golem\" target=\"_blank\">men from clay</a>, so it strikes me as really low level stuff. I'd put it well below summoning a demon of the first circle (which, to be fair, takes a spell). A decent Craft: Clay (Pottery, Brickmaking, Carpentry....) roll to produces some bodies and a Terrestrial Working to produce the Shem, the Words of Life. Repairing the bodies is easy, they are just a lump of earth (the word golem itself comes from &quot;amorphous&quot; or &quot;shapeless&quot;), while being incapacitated means the Shem was damaged, and will need a working to fix.<br /> <br /> In older folklore, golems could actually be killed by a pun! The word on their brow was <i>emet</i> (&quot;Truth&quot;) and removing the <i>e</i> changed it to <i>met</i> (&quot;death&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T19:28:08-07:00","id":1224261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1224259#post1224259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are using the rules for a walking statue/golem/Automaton on page 500 of the rule book, Terrestrial seems sufficient to me. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solomon_ibn_Gabirol\" target=\"_blank\">Folklore</a> is full of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judah_Loew_ben_Bezalel\" target=\"_blank\">people</a> making <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golem\" target=\"_blank\">men from clay</a>, so it strikes me as really low level stuff. I'd put it well below summoning a demon of the first circle (which, to be fair, takes a spell). A decent Craft: Clay (Pottery, Brickmaking, Carpentry....) roll to produces some bodies and a Terrestrial Working to produce the Shem, the Words of Life. Repairing the bodies is easy, they are just a lump of earth (the word golem itself comes from &quot;amorphous&quot; or &quot;shapeless&quot;), while being incapacitated means the Shem was damaged, and will need a working to fix.<br /> <br /> In older folklore, golems could actually be killed by a pun! The word on their brow was <i>emet</i> (&quot;Truth&quot;) and removing the <i>e</i> changed it to <i>met</i> (&quot;death&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the golem!<br /> I'd say making a golem as a working is celestial if its the version that never stops growing.<br /> If its the standard animated statue...Yeah, terrestrial 3 works.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T19:28:53-07:00","id":1224262,"title":"","content":"Robert confirms that the Walking Statue / Golem is NOT an example of the kind of Earth elemental a sorceror can summon. He considers it &quot;about equal&quot; with a Brass Legionnaire, though one seems to be specialized as an elite solo-unit and the other as... well, a member of a legion, meant to obey orders absolutely and fight as part of a unit.<br /> <br /> Individual Brass Legionnaires are Artifact 4; not First Age artifice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another possibility is a riff on Factory Cathedrals.<br /> <br /> Special manses that facilitate the efforts of mortal craftsmen to construct man-shaped effigies of Legendary Size, and the efforts of a Terrestrial sorcerer to enchant such a thing to move with a Celestial working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T19:00:22-07:00","id":1224511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1224262#post1224262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robert confirms that the Walking Statue / Golem is NOT an example of the kind of Earth elemental a sorceror can summon. He considers it &amp;quot;about equal&amp;quot; with a Brass Legionnaire, though one seems to be specialized as an elite solo-unit and the other as... well, a member of a legion, meant to obey orders absolutely and fight as part of a unit.<br /> <br /> Individual Brass Legionnaires are Artifact 4; not First Age artifice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another possibility is a riff on Factory Cathedrals.<br /> <br /> Special manses that facilitate the efforts of mortal craftsmen to construct man-shaped effigies of Legendary Size, and the efforts of a Terrestrial sorcerer to enchant such a thing to move with a Celestial working.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might just be an image thing, but I don't see a lumbering mass of man-shaped-clay as an example of Artifact 4. Its not even A3 for me. It'd make &quot;crude golem&quot; a working. In part because of the image but also mechanically as well. There's really nothing you are getting out of a golem that you couldn't pay someone to do, its just cooler to have a golem do it for you. As meatshields in a palace, it depends what statblock you give them but they are basically dumber, hardier people. For working forges, tilling land, and cleaning rooms it would be an out of pocket expense for most players. <br /> <br /> Watsonian Overlord says : Clay is cheap. <br /> Doyalist Oerlord says : reward the rule of cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T19:42:57-07:00","id":1224521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1224511#post1224511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might just be an image thing, but I don't see a lumbering mass of man-shaped-clay as an example of Artifact 4. Its not even A3 for me. It'd make &quot;crude golem&quot; a working. In part because of the image but also mechanically as well. There's really nothing you are getting out of a golem that you couldn't pay someone to do, its just cooler to have a golem do it for you. As meatshields in a palace, it depends what statblock you give them but they are basically dumber, hardier people. For working forges, tilling land, and cleaning rooms it would be an out of pocket expense for most players.<br /> <br /> Watsonian Overlord says : Clay is cheap.<br /> Doyalist Oerlord says : reward the rule of cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt this the same logic for demons? That would make it more of spell than a working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 06-03-2018, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T19:46:45-07:00","id":1224523,"title":"","content":"How does it stack up to stalwart servitor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:37:50-07:00","id":1224552,"title":"","content":"When thinking about how this would impact the setting, always keep in mind that not every sorcerous working has to be replicable - especially with low finesse. It's not a stretch to say that the clay required to make a player's terracotta army is only found along the shores of a specific water demesne and that - while Realm Sorcerers would love to replicate this en masse - they just can't. This is an important thing to keep in mind when thinking about sorcerous workings. Players are limited by XP. NPCs are limited by in setting reasons a sorcerer might not be able to do things - resources, feuds with local spirit courts, interfering Sidereals, or just raw incompetence are all viable reasons why NPCs aren't just cranking out automaton armies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:43:43-07:00","id":1224556,"title":"","content":"Or maybe they just don't know the particular ritual you did to make the thing happen!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T02:10:46-07:00","id":1224610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1224521#post1224521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isnt this the same logic for demons? That would make it more of spell than a working.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, its a difference of scale. A bloodape is a lot more powerful than a clay golem, and it can think and has charms, on top of that FCD also gets you Agata and Neomah. Spending a whole spell on it is way too much. Besides, one of the example Workings is make Howls Moving Castle with a sentient fire spirit, a task I'd rate waayyyy above golems in difficulty but similar in concept (making the motionless animate). <br /> <br /> If its at the spell level, i would design a spell animating an entire small army of mundane tools, a la *Bedknobs and Broomsticks* (suuub-stituuu-tiary locomotion!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T05:27:28-07:00","id":1224635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1223476-using-sorcery-to-make-war-golems?p=1224610#post1224610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, its a difference of scale. A bloodape is a lot more powerful than a clay golem, and it can think and has charms, on top of that FCD also gets you Agata and Neomah. Spending a whole spell on it is way too much. Besides, one of the example Workings is make Howls Moving Castle with a sentient fire spirit, a task I'd rate waayyyy above golems in difficulty but similar in concept (making the motionless animate).<br /> <br /> If its at the spell level, i would design a spell animating an entire small army of mundane tools, a la *Bedknobs and Broomsticks* (suuub-stituuu-tiary locomotion!)</div> </div> </div> </div>But wouldnt that be more expensive? For the price of one spell you can only make 8-10 golems and it would take you 3 months instead of 8-10 days.<br /> Unless you are talking about a working to make a group of golems. I think that given the nature of spells and workings (workings being unique rituals and spells replicable &quot;techniques&quot;) this type of golem that its supposed to be mass produced its a spell. Of course it could be powered up in some ways, maybe a special power for an essence expenditure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}